{"id":"l5","level":6,"levelName":"Reading literature","n":8,"of":8,"title":"Reading a real page","titleHe":"עַל הַסֵּפֶר","goal":"Put it together on unedited literary Hebrew.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Everything from here is reading. The shelf in the Browse tab is graded by how much of each book is built from the commonest two thousand words — start green and work down."},{"type":"text","body":"Three habits are worth carrying into it."},{"type":"tip","body":"Read to the end of the sentence before you look anything up. Hebrew's verb often arrives late, and half the words you'd have tapped resolve themselves once it does."},{"type":"tip","body":"When a word is unfamiliar, look for the three root letters first. Strip ו, ה, ב, ל, כ, מ, ש from the front and the endings from the back, and what's left is usually something you know."},{"type":"tip","body":"Unvocalized text is the norm outside textbooks and poetry. You'll read it faster than you expect, because context does the work the vowels were doing."}],"vocab":[{"he":"סוֹף","en":"end","translit":"sof"},{"he":"הַתְחָלָה","en":"beginning","translit":"hatchala"},{"he":"מִלָּה","en":"word","translit":"mila"},{"he":"מִשְׁפָּט","en":"sentence","translit":"mishpat"},{"he":"שֹׁרֶשׁ","en":"root","translit":"shoresh"},{"he":"מַשְׁמָעוּת","en":"meaning","translit":"mashma'ut"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["development","part, portion","understanding","end"],"correct":3,"prompt":"סוֹף","translit":"sof"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["beginning","knee","wife, woman","company, society"],"correct":0,"prompt":"הַתְחָלָה","translit":"hatchala"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["word","wave","good","goat"],"correct":0,"prompt":"מִלָּה","translit":"mila"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["money","sentence","computer","Tishrei (Sept–Oct)"],"correct":1,"prompt":"מִשְׁפָּט","translit":"mishpat"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["only","root","inheritance, estate","wind, spirit"],"correct":1,"prompt":"שֹׁרֶשׁ","translit":"shoresh"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["meaning","bank","tractate","anger"],"correct":0,"prompt":"מַשְׁמָעוּת","translit":"mashma'ut"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “root”?","options":["זְאֵב","שֹׁרֶשׁ","בֵּינְתַיִם","אַךְ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["מַשְׁמָעוּת","שֹׁרֶשׁ","מִלָּה","הַתְחָלָה"],"correct":0,"say":"מַשְׁמָעוּת","he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["סוֹף","end"],["הַתְחָלָה","beginning"],["מִלָּה","word"],["מִשְׁפָּט","sentence"],["שֹׁרֶשׁ","root"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “beginning”?","options":["נָקִי","הַתְחָלָה","גִּיל","מֻכָּן"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “meaning”?","options":["בֵּית כְּנֶסֶת","בָּהִיר","מַשְׁמָעוּת","בֵּיתוֹ"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"מִלָּה","translit":"mila","en":"word"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “end”?","options":["גֹּדֶל","פֶּה","סוֹף","עָנָן"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “root” in Hebrew","answer":"שֹׁרֶשׁ","hint":"shoresh"}]}